  "title": "Soft-TransFormers for Continual Learning",
  "summary": "Soft-TransFormers introduces a continual learning framework that adapts a pre-trained Transformer through task-specific soft subnetworks using real-valued masks to control parameter drift and improve performance in real-world scenarios. It achieves a balanced trade-off between model performance and inference cost, while structurally eliminating forgetting and decoupling class-incremental accuracy from task-inference reliability.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Soft-TF uses real-valued multiplicative masks to adapt a frozen pre-trained Transformer.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
